Statements:
[
    "Prompt versioning is vital because prompts are the primary inputs that shape how an LLM responds.",
    "As you improve prompts and system prompts, you must record each version, what changed, and why.",
    "This enables reproducibility, safer rollbacks, and better governance in production.",
    "You have a campus chatbot.",
    "Version 1 prompts the model to "explain in simple terms".",
    "After testing with students, you tweak it to also include examples.",
    "Versioning lets you compare outcomes between v1 and v2 and roll back if v2 makes answers too long or confusing.",
    "You add a grounding instruction (how to use retrieved context) to a prompt.",
    "You create version 2 with that instruction and test it.",
    "If user satisfaction drops, you can revert to version 1 or adjust version 2 and document the change.",
    "You adjust a fallback mechanism for queries outside the knowledge base.",
    "Versioning records the change, the rationale, and the tested results, so you can audit why a particular fallback was chosen.",
    "Experiment tracking is vital because an LLM app (especially a RAG/chatbot) has many moving parts and many possible configurations.",
    "Tracking experiments lets you know which combinations worked best, why, and under what conditions, enabling efficient, data-driven improvements and safe deployment.",
    "You compare multiple document loaders (e.g., different PDF loaders) and chunking strategies.",
    "Experiment tracking records retrieval accuracy and latency for each combo, helping you pick the most reliable setup.",
    "You test different embedding models.",
    "Tracking results show which model yields more accurate or grounded results in your domain.",
    "You test two fallback approaches (direct answer vs. ask for clarification).",
    "Tracking metrics like user satisfaction and rate of helpful responses shows which approach performs better in practice.",
    "You run A/B tests across prompt versions on real users.",
    "Experiment tracking ties each user interaction to the exact prompt version and context used, enabling precise attribution of improvements or regressions.",
    "In short: prompt versioning provides traceable evolution of how your LLM behaves.",
    "Experiment tracking provides the structured record of what you tried, under which conditions, and with what results.",
    "Both are essential for reliable, scalable, and auditable LLM Ops in production."
] 

